        "original_id": "e8ff7b10-c2f9-556f-8d92-f5cdd00b5379",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Bill McCollum, Bill Clinton\n- Events: Impeachment of Bill Clinton, Clinton Senate trial\n- Organizations: U.S. House of Representatives, U.S. Senate\n- Roles: President of the United States\n\nFacts:\n- On December 19, 1998, the U.S. House of Representatives initiated the impeachment of Bill Clinton, the 42nd President of the United States, on charges of perjury and obstruction of justice.\n- Bill McCollum voted to impeach President Bill Clinton.\n- Bill McCollum subsequently took a leadership role in managing Bill Clinton's trial in the U.S. Senate.\n- Bill Clinton's Senate trial ended in acquittal.",
